# Ascentix Rules Engine - environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` in the repo root and fill in the values for YOUR environment. `.env` is
# gitignored and must never be committed; this file is the committed documentation of what
# the project reads.
#
# Resolution order for every key below is the same everywhere: the process environment first,
# then this repo-root `.env`; it is read through client/scripts/devOrg.mjs (`readEnvFile` /
# `envOr`). Nothing is defaulted to a real environment - an unset key fails loudly and names
# itself.
#
# Nothing here is required to build the solution or to run the hermetic unit tests
# (`dotnet test`, `npm test`). These values are only needed to talk to a live Dataverse
# environment: the DEV contract suites (`npm run test:dev`), the Playwright e2e suites
# (`npm run test:e2e`), the Tier-C fresh-org runner, and the maintainer's deploy and release
# builds.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- target environment

# The Dataverse environment the live suites and the deploy/release builds target.
# Power Platform admin center -> Environments -> your environment -> Environment URL.
DATAVERSE_URL=https://your-org.crm.dynamics.com/

# The unique name of the solution the deploy and release builds read from and deploy into. Only
# override this if you renamed the solution; the shipped name is the default.
SOLUTION_NAME=AscentixRulesEngine

# OPTIONAL. A pre-minted Dataverse bearer token. When set it wins over the `az account
# get-access-token` mint, which is how the Tier-C runner drives the suites against a fresh org
# without an interactive `az login`. Leave unset for normal local work.
# DATAVERSE_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- application users

# The full-privilege application user (System Administrator) that drives the Standard-channel
# half of the live suites and the deploy builds. Register an app in Entra ID, add it to the
# environment as an application user, and grant it System Administrator.
# Entra ID -> App registrations -> your app: Application (client) ID / Directory (tenant) ID,
# and a client secret from Certificates & secrets.
SERVICE_PRINCIPAL_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
SERVICE_PRINCIPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
SERVICE_PRINCIPAL_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# A SECOND application user holding ONLY the solution-shipped "Rules Engine Author" security
# role and nothing else. The privilege asymmetry between this user and the one above is the
# fixture for the escalation-guard and SyncSteps-gate suites, so it must not be an admin.
AUTHOR_SP_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
AUTHOR_SP_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
AUTHOR_SP_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sample app

# The appmoduleid of the model-driven app that hosts the sample_* tables and the sample_order
# form. Minted per environment, so it cannot be a constant. Read it from the `appid=` query
# parameter in the app's URL, or query `appmodules?$select=appmoduleid,name` on the org.
# Needed only by the Playwright e2e suites that drive a real form save.
SAMPLE_APP_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secondary environments

# A second environment used for install / upgrade / uninstall verification of the MANAGED
# solution on an org that has never seen it. Only the Tier-C runner reads it.
# TIERC_URL=https://your-trial-org.crm.dynamics.com/

# Fallback for TIERC_URL: a non-English-base environment used to verify localized messages and
# a Content-Security-Policy-enabled host. TIERC_URL wins when both are set.
# LOCALIZATION_ENV_URL=https://your-localization-org.crm.dynamics.com/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- release tooling

# The CI organization and project that host the official release build. Read by the
# maintainer's fresh-org verification harness, which is not part of this repository. Not
# needed for anything else.
# ADO_ORG_URL=https://dev.azure.com/your-organization
# ADO_PROJECT=Your Project Name

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- set by the runners, not by you
#
# These are passed into child processes by CI and by the maintainer's fresh-org harness.
# Setting them in .env has no useful effect. They are listed so the full set of variables the
# code reads is documented:
#   TIERC_RULE_NAME      name of the throwaway rule a fresh-org step arms
#   TIERC_RULE_MESSAGE   the block message that rule carries
#   TIERC_EXPECT         JSON inventory the import-assertions step checks against
#   TIERC_DEV_DRY_RUN    "1" relaxes the fresh-org assertions for a dry run against DEV
#   CI                   set by the build agent; suites use it to skip interactive paths
